-- title:
--   Decomposition-stable admissible small constants for q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number which is prime, assumed equal to $3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ belongs to `A.nonunits`, i.e. $q \in A$ and $q$ is not a unit of $A$. Then there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$, such that, writing $A_0$ for the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, $A_0$ is a henselian local ring, and the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; moreover every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to (the image of) some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$; and $k_0$ is stable under every $\mathbb Q$-automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying $x \in A \iff \tau x \in A$ for all $x$. Finally there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a unit $u$ of $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The field $k_0$ is a field of "small constants" for $A$: a decomposition-stable subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose intersection with $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field carrying all the residues of $A$, equipped with a uniformiser, a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity for an auxiliary prime $\ell$ prime to $qM'$, and a $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$ up to a unit. This is the $q = 3$ instance, used in the construction of Igusa-type smooth point charts on the relevant modular curves and in the companion existence statement for admissible small constants at $q = 3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_admissible_smallConstants_stable_of_eq_three.lean

